            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Criticism and Debate</strong><br>\nThroughout history, Zeno's paradoxes have faced criticism and sparked debate. Many have tried to resolve the paradoxes using calculus and the concept of limits. Despite this, there is still no universally accepted solution, and his paradoxes continue to challenge thinkers across various disciplines.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Zeno's Legacy</strong><br>\nZeno's legacy as a philosopher is marked by his deep influence on the fields of metaphysics and logic. His work is considered a pivotal point in the history of philosophical thought, prompting new ways of questioning and understanding the reality around us.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Relevance Today</strong><br>\nToday, Zeno's paradoxes are still relevant, as they serve as a foundation for philosophical and mathematical inquiry. They encourage students and scholars to question the nature of reality and to understand the limitations and scope of human knowledge and perception.</p>\n"
              },
